{
 "note": "Crank throw 3 is solved exactly as `fea.case_crank` (same solid, load, bearing-reaction supports, standard 1.0 mm mesh along both pin-groove circles and both main-fillet circles, CG solver), then again with extra local refinement in two balls (default radius 3 mm), one on the pin-groove peak and one on the main-fillet peak of the standard mesh, at 0.7 / 0.5 / 0.35 mm - both balls in the same mesh.  For each feature: converged (criterion of the user, 2026-11-23) when its peak in its refined ball changes by less than 5 % between the two finest meshes; otherwise NOT CONVERGED and only the series is reported (no value is picked).  The feature peak is the maximum over ball and feature zone (the zones of `fea.crank_zones`), so a stress outside the feature cannot be taken for it; the zone peak outside the ball must stay below the refined peak.  Decision rule of the user (D-050): if the converged main-fillet factor is below 1.5, the main fillets switch to option (b) (R2.5 on the journal with narrower main shells).  Each run also gives the web and the ligament stresses (web 9.5 mm, 7.0 mm remaining behind the 2.5 mm groove).  Each record carries the pin bore and the main fillet radius it was solved with; earlier records (hollow pin, fixed journals, no main fillets) are kept under their own keys.",
